-- title:
--   Below-one state Rényi divergence converges under faithful approximation
-- statement:
--   Let $\rho,\sigma$ be density operators on a nonzero finite-dimensional complex Hilbert space and let $0<p<1$. Set $\rho_\lambda=(1-\lambda)\rho+\lambda I/\dim H$ and $\sigma_\lambda=(1-\lambda)\sigma+\lambda I/\dim H$. Then
--
--   $$\widetilde D_p(\rho_\lambda\Vert\sigma_\lambda)\longrightarrow\widetilde D_p(\rho\Vert\sigma)\quad\text{as }\lambda\downarrow0,\quad0<\lambda\le1.$$
--
--   The divergence is in bits and convergence uses the extended-real order topology. No support inclusion is assumed; an orthogonal-support target can be infinite. This extends faithful-state comparisons to all density states below order one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/JWang226/Continuity-of-regularized-channel-renyi-divergence/blob/e29274a69978bb499f00497481c6008befb0b84d/QuantumChannelContinuity/StateOrderBoundary.lean#L105-L145

